Camera Calibration - Complete Notes for AI Engineering

Camera calibration is one of the most important topics in Computer Vision, 
Robotics, Autonomous Vehicles, AR/VR, 3D Reconstruction, and AI Engineering. 
It helps determine how a camera maps 3D real-world points to 2D image points.

1. Introduction to Camera Calibration
What is Camera Calibration?

Camera calibration is the process of estimating the intrinsic and extrinsic parameters of a camera.

It answers:

How does the camera see the world?
What are the camera's internal characteristics?
Where is the camera located in the world?
How are image distortions corrected?
Real-World Example

Suppose a robot sees an object in an image at pixel coordinates:

(650, 350)


To pick up that object, the robot needs its real-world position:

(2.4 m, 1.1 m, 0.6 m)


Calibration provides the mathematical relation between image coordinates and world coordinates.

