11. Why Objects Appear Smaller Far Away

Consider two points:

Point 1
(X,Y,Z)=(1,1,5)(X,Y,Z)=(1,1,5) x=15=0.2x=\frac{1}{5}=0.2
Point 2
(X,Y,Z)=(1,1,20)(X,Y,Z)=(1,1,20) x=120=0.05x=\frac{1}{20}=0.05

As ZZ increases:

x,y→0x,y \rightarrow 0

Hence distant objects shrink toward the image center.

This creates perspective.

