Final Master Equation

The complete mathematical model of image formation is:

s[uv1]=[fx0cx0fycy001]⏟Intrinsic[Rt]⏟Extrinsic[XwYwZw1]\boxed{ s \begin{bmatrix} u\\ v\\ 1 \end{bmatrix} = \underbrace{ \begin{bmatrix} f_x &0&c_x\\ 0&f_y&c_y\\ 0&0&1 \end{bmatrix} }_{\text{Intrinsic}} \underbrace{ \begin{bmatrix} R&t \end{bmatrix} }_{\text{Extrinsic}} \begin{bmatrix} X_w\\ Y_w\\ Z_w\\ 1 \end{bmatrix} }

This single equation describes how every 3D point in the world is mapped onto a 2D camera image and forms the foundation of camera calibration, SLAM, Structure-from-Motion (SfM), 3D reconstruction, and modern computer vision systems.
  
